h("2. Archive, queues and configuration")
p("The local Reviewer data directory contains archive, Logs, InBox/InBoxWork variants, notificationQueue, syslogQueue, Rejects, es7 and reviewerconfig.db. This establishes that Reviewer has service-managed working storage outside the Python project. Folder names alone do not establish the size or detailed processing behavior of each queue. [L3]")
p("The automation verified the selected UHH against a matching archive file under C:\\ProgramData\\Eurotherm\\Reviewer\\archive. The installed vendor README, HA033274 Issue 5.3, page 14, also identifies ProgramData\\Eurotherm\\Reviewer as containing archived UHH files and logs. [L1, L5]")
h("3. Why C: was selected originally")
p("The evidence establishes the current paths, but does not identify the installation decision-maker. They may have been chosen by installation defaults, an installer workflow or an administrator. The reviewed files do not prove which of those occurred. No claim is made that Reviewer must use C: on every installation.")
p("The inspected Reviewer API assembly reports version 5.3.0. Storage relocation must therefore be checked against the supported procedure for this installed product/version, not assumed from a generic Windows or Elasticsearch example. [L6]")
h("General indexing background")
p("Elastic’s documentation distinguishes the indexed data directory from its own application-log directory and describes path.data and path.logs as the settings controlling those locations. That explains the role of the two local entries above; it is not a Eurotherm migration authorization. [W2]")

