h("The output folder does not control the database")
p("REPORT_OUTPUT_DIR and DOWNLOAD_DIR configure the automation’s report destinations. They are not Reviewer database-location settings. PROJECT_ROOT, the virtual environment and the script’s temporary directory likewise do not relocate an already installed Windows service’s data store. [L4]")
h("What is confirmed about the failure")
p("The failure log shows that the application was accessible, the selected file was already imported, and group/archive matching succeeded. Reviewer then reported low disk space and indexing disabled; the automation stopped before chart/Preview/PDF operations. This confirms a preflight refusal. It does not prove that every manual read-only screen or every manual report operation is unavailable. [L1]")
h("An independent date-range problem")
p("The selected Group 6 recording ends on 1 August 2026. The configured environment interval requests 8–9 October 2026 at +01:00, which does not overlap that recording. Historical test mode selects available August data and removes that missing-interval issue, but does not remove the disk/indexing blockers. Freeing space alone does not create missing October samples. [L1, L7]")

page("What the 5 GB minimum means", 4)
h("The value comes from Reviewer’s status")
p("The native Reviewer status result contained these fields. The automation reads the configured minimum; it does not calculate or set 5 GB. No setting was changed during this investigation. [L1, L4]")
table(["Status field", "Captured value", "Meaning"], [
    ("freeDiskSize", "2.0616912841796875", "Free capacity reported by Reviewer."),
    ("settings_MinFreeDiskSpace", "5", "Reviewer’s reported minimum free-space setting."),
    ("indexingEnable", "false", "Reviewer reports indexing disabled."),
    ("diskStatus", "ErrorDiskFull", "Reviewer disk error state; not necessarily zero bytes free."),
    ("elasticStatus", "ErrorDiskFull", "Related indexing-service error state reported by Reviewer."),
    ("D: free, Windows query", "187.19 GB approximately", "Capacity on the PDF/output volume; separate from C:."),
], [3500, 2400, 4000])
p("At this snapshot, 5 − 2.0617 = approximately 2.94 GB of additional free capacity would reach the reported minimum. Restoring more than the exact shortfall gives operating headroom; an amount selected for long-term retention needs a separate capacity review. Values are labelled GB by the application; the Python Windows-disk helper divides bytes by 1024³, technically GiB.")
h("Who set it?")
p("The logs do not identify who selected the threshold or when it changed. It could originate in product defaults or site administration, but neither origin is established here. Installation records, the applicable manual or configuration audit history are needed to answer that ownership question.")
h("Three different concepts must stay separate")
p("Reviewer’s observed 5 GB operational setting is distinct from vendor installation capacity guidance. The installed README lists 60 GB free disk space for Foundation Edition system requirements; that is planning guidance, not proof of the origin of the 5 GB setting. [L5, W1]")
p("Elasticsearch has its own disk-allocation settings. The inspected local YAML contains cluster.routing.allocation.disk.threshold_enabled: false. This is a file observation, not a live cluster-settings query. It does not establish a live effective value, and does not disable or explain away Reviewer’s separately reported minimum. [L2, W3]")

page("What changing the PDF location can and cannot fix", 5)
h("Changing only the output directory")
p("Keeping PDFs on D: is useful because finished reports then consume D: capacity. It does not move existing archives, indexed data, service logs, queues, installed binaries or Windows-managed files. The same principle applies to keeping Python code and its temporary files under D:\\Ceiyone.")
